-- title:
--   The Čech complex of free abelian sheaves attached to a morphism, its augmentation, and the extra degeneracy on sections
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal C$ be a category with finite wide pullbacks, equipped with a Grothendieck topology $J$ for which abelian sheafification exists, and let $f : V \to U$ be a morphism. Write $\mathbb Z[X]$ for the free abelian presheaf on the (universe-lifted) representable presheaf of $X$, and $\mathbb Z[X]^{\#}$ for its sheafification. This file defines:
--
--   - the *Čech complex of free abelian presheaves* of $f$: the chain complex with $n$-th term $\mathbb Z[V\times_U\cdots\times_U V]$ ($n+1$ factors) and differential the alternating sum of the face maps of the Čech nerve;
--   - the *Čech complex of free abelian sheaves*, its sheafification, with terms $\check C_n = \mathbb Z[V^{\times_U (n+1)}]^{\#}$, differentials $d_n : \check C_{n+1} \to \check C_n$, and the augmentation $\varepsilon : \check C_0 = \mathbb Z[V]^{\#} \to \mathbb Z[U]^{\#}$ induced by $f$.
--
--   Results proved:
--
--   1. $d_n \circ d_{n+1} = 0$ and $\varepsilon \circ d_0 = 0$, i.e. one has a complex
--   $$\cdots \to \mathbb Z[V\times_U V]^{\#} \to \mathbb Z[V]^{\#} \xrightarrow{\ \varepsilon\ } \mathbb Z[U]^{\#} \to 0.$$
--   2. The free-presheaf augmentation factors through the free abelian presheaf on the sieve generated by $f$.
--   3. For each object $W$, the Čech nerve of $f$ evaluated at $W$, augmented over the set of morphisms $W \to U$ factoring through $f$, is isomorphic to the Čech nerve (in sets) of the surjection $\operatorname{Hom}(W,V) \to \{g : W\to U \text{ factoring through } f\}$; it therefore has an extra degeneracy, and the evaluated free abelian Čech complex is homotopy equivalent to the free abelian group on that set, placed in degree $0$.
--   4. Routine lemmas on factorization through $f$, on projections and base maps of the Čech nerve, and the compatibility of the differentials with evaluation.
--
--   The module docstring announces that the augmented complex is a resolution of $\mathbb Z[U]^{\#}$ when $f$ generates a covering sieve; these are the ingredients for that statement (pointwise exactness via the extra degeneracy), which is the key input for comparing Čech cohomology with derived-functor cohomology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The category is `C : Type (u+1)` with `Category.{u} C`, and abelian groups are `AddCommGrpCat.{u+1}`. Main declarations: `CategoryTheory.freeAbelianPresheafFunctor`, `cechFreePresheafComplex`, `cechFreeComplex`, `cechFree` (with `cechFree_eq` identifying it with `freeAbelianSheafFunctor J` applied to the Čech nerve object), `cechFreeD`, `cechFreeAug`, `cechFreeD_comp_d`, `cechFreeD_comp_aug`, `cechNerveEvalAugIso`, `cechNerveEvalED`, `cechFreeEvalHomotopyEquiv`. The exactness of the sheafified complex and the epimorphy of the augmentation are not proved in this file.
